ADR-0012 G2c-2 step 7 (owner-visible): the Workers Builds build script posts the Console dist to the Forge.

Proposed patch, not committed. workers/forge-typecheck/** is an owner-only harness path. Apply from the
repository root with `git apply step7-console-dist.patch` on top of the step 6 commit.

- typecheck-and-report.mjs: on a build of main (WORKERS_CI_BRANCH `main`, or empty for an Artifacts build of
  main) whose Console UI built, walk workers/console/ui/dist, POST /v1/forge/console-dist with the same headers
  as postReport (content-type, CF-Access-Client-Id, CF-Access-Client-Secret, redirect: "manual") and the body
  { confirm: "UPLOAD", commit, files: [{ path, content_base64, content_type }] }, before the report. A 3xx is a
  refused token; anything but a JSON 200 naming the build's commit fails. A failed dist post still posts the
  report (the Orchestrator keeps the Console on its workflow: console_dist_missing) and exits 3. A dist over the
  Forge's 36 MiB request limit is refused locally, never sent. Content types follow ADR-0012 §5l item 7.
- typecheck-and-report.d.mts: declarations of the new exports.
- README.md: the dist post in "How it works".
- forge-console-dist-g2c2.test.ts: FD4 now asserts the script posts the dist before the report (it asserted
  that the script does not post yet); FD5 tests the new functions (content types, the branch rule, the walk
  accepted by the Forge's validateConsoleDist, headers and body, 3xx/409/mismatch/non-JSON refused, the size
  limit).

Checked on a scratch copy with this patch applied: control-plane-shared tests 603/0, tsc --noEmit clean,
node tools/forge-runner/run.mjs passed (603/0, bundles 13/13).

